thread:
maria: Heads-up — planning to ship audit-events schema v3 tomorrow morning. Major diffs: added event.source.ip, kms.key_id, rbac.action; actor.id is canonicalized. Need docs, changelog, and a customer-facing validation harness updated ASAP.

aj: Do we have a migration strategy? Will we dual-write v2/v3 or strict switch?

maria: Dual-write for 48h then flip validation to v3-only. We'll include event.version so consumers can detect. Snippet of new canonical event: 
```json
{
  "event": {
    "version": "3",
    "type": "policy.change",
    "actor": {
      "id": "user|12345",
      "display_name": "aj"
    },
    "rbac": {
      "action": "grant_role",
      "resource": "project:alpha"
    },
    "kms": {
      "key_id": "proj-alpha:cmk-01ab23"
    },
    "source": {
      "ip": "198.51.100.23"
    }
  }
}
```

kevin: Quick flag — exposing full key_id in customer-visible audit events may concern SOC. Recommend partial redaction or hashing for external-facing logs.

sarah: For customer validation, propose a POST /audit/validate that accepts sample payloads and returns schema issues + friendly hints. Also we should publish a migration guide and a changelog entry that calls out canonicalization as a potential breaking change.

jordan: RBAC implications: new rbac.action values mean role mappings in the console need updates. Ops will need a short migration for role editors and API tokens.

deploy-bot: deploy-bot: audit-schema-service v3 rolling to staging at 12:10 UTC — health checks pending.

maria: Assigning owners: @sarah owns customer comms and the validator UX, @kevin owns KMS redaction review, @aj handles rollout gating and CI tests. Please confirm.

sarah: I can own comms. Draft will include impact summary, sample events, validator link, and a clear rollback path. I’ll post to #announcements by EOD.

aj: I’ll add a canary that sends v3 events to a test webhook and validate the schema. Also will run a quick vuln triage: primary risk is PII leakage via source.ip and key_id. Suggest masking IPs in public docs.

kevin: I’ll run KMS access audit and propose a redaction format (keep last 6 chars hashed). Will file a security PR with details.

maria: Final checklist before GA: docs PR, changelog entry, validator endpoint, KMS redaction implemented, RBAC console mapping updated, QA canary green. Ping me when your PRs are up. :thumbsup:

aj: Will do.

maria: Thanks team — prioritize comms for mid-market customers that use dedicated/private modes (they care about key_id semantics).

sarah: Noted — will add a short FAQ for Dedicated/Private regarding KMS visibility.

maria: Closing loop here. If any blocker emerges during staging rollout, post in this thread and tag me.
